// Back assassination, one point of the sweep over distance (300 uu behind an unaware guard, both
// facing -x). Original (melee.md): DisItemContext_Assassinate, m_fMaxContextRange 275, target must be an
// NPC whose awareness is one of the m_AssassinateOnAwareness states (0, 2, 3, 6), not running unless
// m_bCanAssassinateRunners; any direction (Front / Back / Left / Right move sets). The port allows only the back
// cone (+-60 deg), 165 uu (0.6 x 275), view within 45 deg. A Passive (no AI) dummy has an unknown original
// awareness, so the expected value is UNMEASURED.
(
    name: "combat/melee_assassinate_back_d300",
    system: Combat,
    map: "Playground",
    description: "Swing at an unaware guard 300 uu ahead of the player, both facing the same way.",
    setup: (
        player: Some((position: (-5300, 0, 96), yaw: 180, pitch: 0)),
        npcs: [(id: Some("dummy"), position: Some((-5600, 0, 92)), yaw: 180, state: Some("Passive"))],
        settle: 30,
    ),
    ticks: 180,
    input: [(tick: 5, action: Press(Primary))],
    checkpoints: [
        (name: "assassinated", expect: [(metric: Count("Sim:Death@dummy[cause=Assassination]"), value: 0, tol: 0, source: "context range 275 (original design reading); port 165", status: Unmeasured)]),
    ],
    record: [Pawn, Npc("dummy"), SimEvents],
    capture: Some("lab npcs; place the player 300 uu behind an unaware guard (idle, not passive); press attack; record the context chosen (DisItemContext_Assassinate vs MeleeAttackPlayer) and the target's awareness value"),
